1.bug_scenario:
When using the “ignoreRestSiblings” option on the no-unused-vars rule, it correctly suppresses “unused” warnings for siblings in a variable destructuring assignment (e.g. const { x, ...rest } = obj), but it does not suppress the warning when the destructuring appears in a function parameter. In code like

  const MyComp = ({ children, ...props }) => {
    return <OtherComp {...props} />;
  };

ESLint still warns “'children' is defined but never used,” even though ignoreRestSiblings was set to true.
